    <name>
      <text>irrational numbers 1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Simplify \(\sqrt{@number@}\) to the simplest form.</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>To simplify \( \sqrt{ {@number@} } \), look for the largest perfect-square factor of {@number@}.</p>
<p>Since {@number@} = {@a@} × {@b@}, and {@a@} is a perfect square:</p>
<p>\[ \sqrt{ {@number@} } = \sqrt{ {@a@} } \times \sqrt{ {@b@} } = {@sqrt(a)@}\sqrt{ {@b@} } \]</p>
<p><strong>Key idea:</strong> an irrational number is fully simplified when the number left under the root sign has no perfect-square factors remaining. Always check for the largest such factor first otherwise you may simplify only part-way.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
